  clock: 2  # a89d
  nonce: a89d  # a89d
  message: "P4 REVIEW 2026-11-01 (dev 9ae4abe13f; owner-requested re-check of open P4 items last modified before 2026-10-20; fixtures under ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/p4_review_11012026/links1/). VERDICT: PARTLY-STALE. Re-checked 2026-11-01 at 9ae4abe13f. The node: slot-leak half is fixed by WI-fiham (1b66138525, 2026-10-03), which strips the scheme on import, require and attribute-read edges. A NO-SUBPROC claim on import http from 'node:http' with http.STATUS_CODES now reports \"(http)\", not node:http (http itself is deliberately withheld from a grant). The os half reproduces: const os = require('os') with os.EOL and os.hostname() gives NO-SUBPROC inconclusive \"could not classify (os)\". javascript.yaml module_completeness still has no os entry. MECHANISM: module rows without a completeness grant: the uncatalogued-module rung counts a module whose called name has no row."  # a89d
